# #1002: requested tool names/actions are not permission grants.
# Every mapped system operation needs the corresponding authoritative permission
# for its actual target. Indirect evidence/POAM IDs resolve their stored owner;
# a caller cannot authorize another owner's artifact by supplying an allowed ID.
# Unknown tools/actions fail closed. Provider/support read oversight does not
# imply write or approval authority.
#
# Chat system tools require an explicitly selected, validated system matching the
# actual tool target. System-free chat may use only mapped public reference tools:
# it must not put system data into an unbound persistent AI thread.
# Workspace chat bypasses response caching so every turn executes authorization.
#
# Required shared hook: BaseTool.ExecuteAsync must demand the request-scoped
# ToolExecutionAuthorization after canonical system-ID resolution and before
# ExecuteCoreAsync. MCP supplies the policy through an async-flow-local scope;
# no mutable singleton tool properties or global-role elevation are used.
# Only /mcp, /mcp/chat and /mcp/chat/stream carry the self-authorizing workspace
# marker. Their authenticated workspace resolution and shared execution guard
# remain mandatory; unrelated POSTs receive no broader admission.
# Next reviewed slice: explicit system reads for baseline, categorization,
# profile/completeness, roadmap, imports, boundaries, inventory, privacy,
# interconnections, POAM and SAP. Read renderers do not persist an artifact.
# Optional metrics system IDs are REQUIRED in workspace calls (no unbounded
# aggregate). Control-validation permits only default/get, never add/delete.
# Import/item/SAP/component IDs resolve their persisted system. Boundary,
# component, assessment and import-array filters must agree with that system.
# AO issuance and risk acceptance require CanDecideAuthorization and every
# finding's assessment owner must match the requested system. Inline inputs use
# the native RiskAcceptanceInput JSON contract (camelCase/PascalCase).
# Approved integrity verification: effective assigned SCA OR CanManageEvidence,
# evaluated for the evidence's persisted assessment/system owner. This does not
# confer assessment approval or evidence-authoring authority. A qualified
# verifier and atomic audit are enforced by the domain service as well as MCP.
# Evidence completeness is a read: optional assessment must belong to the
# selected system, and evidence aggregates exclude other systems/unowned rows.
# Still denied pending narrow domain decisions: SCA assessment recording,
# snapshot creation, SAP mutations, SAR mutations,
# queued package generation, cross-system bundle lookup, cloud/PIM operations.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@token = REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_TEST_TOKEN
@organization = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@system = REPLACE_WITH_AUTHORIZED_SYSTEM_ID
@evidence = REPLACE_WITH_OWNED_COMPLIANCE_EVIDENCE_ID

### Evidence integrity only: SCA or authorized evidence manager, not a browser role
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{organization}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": "verify-integrity",
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "compliance_verify_evidence",
    "arguments": { "evidence_id": "{{evidence}}" }
  }
}

### Authoring: requires actual CanAuthorNarratives, not read permission
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{organization}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "narrative_set_policy",
    "arguments": {
      "system_id": "{{system}}",
      "control_id": "AC-1",
      "policy_narrative": "Synthetic local test narrative"
    }
  }
}

### Unknown operations must be denied even for a global administrator
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Workspace-Kind: organization
X-Workspace-Tenant-Id: {{organization}}
X-Workspace-Mode: ordinary
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 2,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "unmapped_mutator",
    "arguments": { "system_id": "{{system}}", "user_role": "CSP.Admin" }
  }
}
